{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Mi6ELxGgnMw6uX15mH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] SSR suite: `html` with an unclosed void element that has children throws, and the error message contains the tag name.\n[x] SSR suite: `html` with the same void element self-closed does not throw and emits no closing tag (existing behaviour kept).\n[x] SSR suite: static pages used by the exact-string assertions stay byte-identical.\n[x] Browser suite: the browser `html` throws on a void element with children, and the error message contains the tag name.\n[x] Browser suite: `mount` of markup with self-closed void elements still creates them (existing void-element test still passes).\n\nBoth templaters now throw when a void element gets children, so an unclosed tag like `<input type=\"text\">` stops silently swallowing the rest of a page. Final run: SSR suite 83/83, browser suite 291/291, lint clean.\n\nThe error names the tag and its self-closing form, and says that an unclosed void element swallows what follows it. Any child counts, including whitespace. The check is at the top of `h` in `src/htm.ts` and `src/htm.browser.ts`. It's written out in both files instead of shared, the same way the two `VOID` sets are, which are unchanged.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **SSR:** an unclosed `<input>` with a following element throws naming `input`, and `<br>` followed by just a space throws naming `br`. A self-closed `<input />` keeps the content after it. The existing exact-string static-page test still passes.\n- **Browser:** the browser `html` throws on an unclosed `<input>` naming `input`.\n- **Ticket mismatch:** the ticket assumes a browser test already mounts void elements, but the only existing one goes through the server `html`. So I added a `mount` test with self-closed `<input />` and `<br />`. It passed before my change, so it only pins down how things already worked.\n\n**Docs:**\n- The README \"Void elements\" paragraph now says the templater throws on the server and in the browser.\n- AGENTS.md gains two notes. The first says the two `VOID` sets must stay identical. The second says tapzero's `t.throws` returns a promise and must be awaited, or the assertion lands after the test ends.\n\nThings the next ticket should know:\n- **Build first:** a fresh worktree needs `npm run build` before `npm test`, because typecheck resolves `microtags` through `dist/`.\n- **Port clash:** port 8123 clashed with another worktree's run, so I retried until it was free.\n- **`example/ssr.ts`:** it has unclosed `<meta>` and `<link>` tags, but in a plain string rather than `html`, so the new check doesn't affect it.\n\nThere are three commits, and `.nightralph/notes.md` is left uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":66237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":267},"output_tokens":678,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4ebf683-756f-4f71-90e5-ea0c6aa2a231","uuid":"8041dddd-8cd9-44b5-af24-27d43d9b4045","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:02:45.839Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Mi5sm28rnKv64ntBnP"}
